@*
    The inline error region: what a surface says when a submission comes back rejected.

    role="alert" AND tabindex="-1" AND FOCUS MOVED TO IT. All three, and the third is the one that
    was nearly missed. review-accessibility.md:62 records a critical review finding that rejected
    exactly the shape this could have been: "a bare aria-live region with no focus move". An alert
    region announces itself once, to a screen reader, and then the person is still standing on
    whichever control they submitted from - with no way to reach the message, no way to re-read
    it, and no idea where it is. Moving focus puts them at the message.

    tabindex="-1" makes it a programmatic focus target without adding it to the tab order, which
    would be worse: a static message a keyboard user has to tab THROUGH on every pass is a
    permanent tax for a transient event. base.css excludes [tabindex="-1"] from the 24px target
    floor for exactly this reason - it is not a pointer target, so WCAG 2.5.8 does not apply.

    The focus move happens on FIRST RENDER of this component, so the caller controls when it
    fires by keying the element on the attempt number: a new attempt is a new instance, and a new
    instance re-announces and re-focuses. Without that, a second failed attempt would render into
    the existing region and say nothing at all.
*@

<div class="form-status" role="alert" tabindex="-1" @ref="_region">
    <p class="form-status__heading">@Heading</p>

    @if (Messages.Count > 0)
    {
        <ul class="form-status__list">
            @foreach (var message in Messages)
            {
                <li>@message</li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private ElementReference _region;

    /// <summary>
    /// The region's opening line, announced first. Always a resource lookup.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public string Heading { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// One line per problem, already resolved to localised text by the caller.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Messages { get; set; } = [];

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            await _region.FocusAsync();
        }
    }
}
